-- title:
--   Descent of the q+1 nodes to the fixed field, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=2$, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Further data: a valuation subring $A$ of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`); a finite set $W$ of places of $\operatorname{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over the residue field of $A$, whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. the rational places of the affine geometric locus at which the value of the generator $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$ — the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic curve with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero $q$-torsion point (`hW`); a distinguished $s \in W$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of the base-changed modular function field $\operatorname{modularFunctionFieldBar} M'$ to $\operatorname{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ relative to $A$ (a valuation subring of integers, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, compatibility with $A$ on constants and a degree-preserving place map), assumed compatible with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$ (`hR₀`), together with the inclusion $\operatorname{modularFunctionFieldBar} M' \le \operatorname{fieldBar} q\,M'$ (`hle`); a number field $k_0$ inside the algebraic closure, an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, and the induced valuation ring $A_0 := A.\mathrm{comap}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ k_0\ \overline{\mathbb{Q}})$.
--
--   The base hypotheses on $A$ and $A_0$ are: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field (`hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`), and every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hκ`). Auxiliary arithmetic data, all used only through the quoted hypotheses: a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$, an element $\varpi_t' \in A_0$ with $\varpi_t' = \varpi_t$, an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0$ in the algebraic closure with $K_b = \bot$ carrying a valuation subring $A_b$ cut out by $A$ and a non-zero generator $\varpi_b$ of its maximal ideal, the tameness assumption that $(\ell_g-1)/2$ is a unit of $A_0$ (`htame`), and a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi \in k_0$.
--
--   The level data are: $H_1 = \operatorname{levelH} q\,M' \sqcap \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times\big)$ (`hH₁`), the intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0$ in the Laurent series field over $k_0$ with $K_\ell = \operatorname{laurentBaseChange} k_0\,(\operatorname{xHFunctionField} (q^2M')\,H_1)$ (`hKℓ`), equipped with compatible $A_0$-algebra and scalar-tower structures, and a non-zero $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ whose Laurent expansion is $\operatorname{coeffEmb} k_0\,\mathrm{jq}$ (`hjℓ`). Here $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$ denotes the subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$, and for $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ the predicate `IsLevelAutAt` $k_0\ q\ \xi\ q\ (q^2M')\ H_1\ \gamma^{-1}\ K_\ell\ \tau$ says that the $k_0$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ implements $\gamma^{-1}$ on $q$-expansions: for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g$ giving a non-zero series, every $x \in K_\ell$ whose Laurent expansion is the quotient of these series, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota \xi = \exp(2\pi i/q)$, the coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$.
--
--   The point of the special fibre is given by a maximal ideal $y$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$ containing $\pi_0$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$ the image of $\mathrm{jChartFin}$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$ (`hss`); lying over $s$ in the sense that for every $g$ in $\operatorname{modularFunctionFieldFull} M'$ that is $R_0$-integral, has no pole where $\mathrm{jq}$ has none, and whose $R_0$-reduction lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at that reduction, the difference of $g$ and $c$ lies in $y$ (`hover`); and such that every maximal ideal of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ with the same property is carried to $y$ by some level automorphism attached to a $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving the chart algebra (`hOrbit`). Moreover $\operatorname{jqNModC} k_0\,q$ lies in $K_\ell$ (`hjK`) and in the chart algebra (`hjC`), and $a_0 \in A_0$ satisfies $\operatorname{jqNModC} k_0\,q - a_0 \in y$ (`ha₀y`).
--
--   The rigid model upstairs is encoded by the following hypothesis groups, each a conjunction of clauses summarised here. The rigid-chart package `hS1` (thirteen clauses) requires: the chart algebra is contained in the $A_0$-subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$, which has fraction field $K_\ell$, is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$ and has $B_t/(\pi_0)$ of Krull dimension at most one; the valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ (containing $B_t$ by `hBW`) induces $A_0$ on $k_0$, is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is the localisation of $B_t$ there, and cuts out $y$ on the chart algebra; for each $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A_0$ there is a surjective homomorphism $\rho$ from $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q$ over that residue field, with kernel the elements of the maximal ideal of $W_t$, compatible with scalars, and equivariant for level automorphisms of $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ through an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma, c)$ of $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ acting by $\mathrm{hAction}$, with $c \ne 1$ for non-trivial automorphisms coming from $\Gamma(q)$ and with every such scalar $c$ also realised by a level automorphism with trivial matrix part; $B_t$ is stable under level automorphisms of $\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is obtained from the maximal ideal of $W_t$ by such an automorphism; and an element of $B_t$ all of whose $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$-translates lie in the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is divisible by $\pi_0$. The deck-group data are $n$ with $1 \le n \mid q+1$ and $n = \operatorname{placeWidthChar} q\,M'\,s$ (`hn1`, `hnq`, `hn`), where $\operatorname{placeWidthChar}$ is $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\,q$ of the value of $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ at the place divided by the ramification index $\operatorname{placeRamificationJ}$, an element $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ with a level automorphism $\tau_0$ at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ preserving $W_t$, an exponent $m \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t'\,w$ for a unit $w$ of $A_0$, and an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ which is a primitive $n$-th root of unity in the strong sense that $\zeta_c^n = 1$ and $\zeta_c^k - 1$ is a unit for $0 < k < n$. The ends package `hR7` (twelve clauses, summarised here) requires: $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B_t$ pointwise while no smaller power does, every level automorphism preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with a power of $\tau_0$; the finite set $\mathrm{ends}$ of subrings of $K_\ell$ has $q+1$ elements, is permuted transitively by the level automorphisms of $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$, is fixed elementwise by $\tau_0$, and its members are pairwise separated by an element which is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; there is a level-stable finite-type subalgebra of which each end is a localisation; a level automorphism mapping an end into $W_t$ preserves $W_t$; each end $O$ is a Noetherian local subring of $W_t$ containing the chart algebra, inducing $A_0$ on $k_0$, with residues represented by scalars, and carries a crossing presentation: $\pi_0 \in O$, elements $c_x c_y = \pi_0^m u$, and an isomorphism of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the adic completion of $A_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^m$ matching constants, sending $c_x, c_y$ to unit multiples of $U$ and $V$, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, with $\operatorname{jqNModC} k_0\,q - a_0$ corresponding to a unit times $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$, and with $\tau_0$ corresponding to an automorphism scaling $U$ by $\zeta_c$ and $V$ by $\zeta_c^{-1}$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal; each end further carries an adapted discrete valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ and an end-adapted level-stable finite-type chart $B_x$ with the separation and pole properties stated there; and finally a dichotomy: a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ inducing $A_0$ on $k_0$, containing the chart algebra and centred at $y$ either contains $B_t$ or is dominated by one of the ends. The two separation hypotheses are `hR9`, the existence of an element of $B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring of $K_\ell$ which induces $A_0$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, and at which no monic $A_0$-polynomial in $j_\ell$ becomes a non-unit; and `hR10`, the corresponding statement for each maximal ideal of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ that is not a level translate of $y$.
--
--   Finally the descent data: $G$ is the subgroup of $k_0$-automorphisms of $K_\ell$ generated by all level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`), $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`), $B_0$ consists of the elements of $B_t$ fixed by $G$ (`hB₀`), and $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ cut out by $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of: a proof that the class of $\mathrm{jq}$ in $\operatorname{modularFunctionFieldBar} M'$ is $R_0$-integral; a proof that its $R_0$-reduction lies in the valuation subring of $s$; a proof that, whenever $a_0$ is viewed in $A$, the $q$-th power of its residue equals the value of $s$ at that reduction; and a finite set $\mathrm{nodes}$ of subrings of $K_0$ such that the following eight assertions hold.
--
--   First, $\mathrm{nodes}$ has exactly $q+1$ elements. Second, there is a subring $B_c$ of $K_0$ which is the subring generated by the image of $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite subset of $K_0$, such that every node contains $B_c$ and is its localisation: $f$ lies in a node $O$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g,h \in B_c$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h \in O$. Third, for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ and every $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$ there is $O' \in \mathrm{nodes}$ with $f \in O \iff \tau f \in O'$ for all $f \in K_\ell$ lying, together with $\tau f$, in $K_0$. Fourth, transitivity: for all $O, O' \in \mathrm{nodes}$ there are $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $f \in O \iff \tau f \in O'$ in the same sense. Fifth, distinct nodes $O \ne O'$ are separated: some $f$ lies in both and is a non-unit of $O$ but a unit of $O'$. Sixth, a dichotomy for valuation subrings $V$ of $K_0$ inducing $A$ on $k_0$ (that is, $x \in A \iff$ the image of $x$ lies in $V$, for $x \in k_0$) and centred at $s$ in the sense that for every $g \in \operatorname{modularFunctionFieldFull} M'$ which is $R_0$-integral, has no pole where $\mathrm{jq}$ has none and whose reduction lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the element $\operatorname{coeffEmb} k_0\,g$ lies in $K_0$ and in $V$, and $g - c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$ for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue matches the value of $s$ at the reduction of $g$: for every such $V$, either all of $B_0$ lies in $K_0$ and in $V$, or some node $O$ is contained in $V$ with all its non-units falling into the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   Seventh and last, for every node $O$: $O$ is contained in $W_0'$; $O$ is a Noetherian local ring; for $x \in k_0$ one has $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $O$; every $f \in O$ differs from the image of some $x \in k_0 \cap A$ lying in $O$ by a non-unit of $O$; and there exist an exponent $E_0 \ge 1$, together with an element $v \in k_0$ with $v$ and $v^{-1}$ in $A$ and $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\operatorname{placeWidthChar} q\,M'\,s}\, v$, the membership $\pi_0 \in O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the adic completion of $A_0$ with parameter the $E_0$-th power of the image of $\pi_0$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that: $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries the image of every $x \in k_0 \cap A$ lying in $O$ to the corresponding constant; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V\,V$; $c_y$ lies in $W_0'$ and in its maximal ideal, while $c_x$, when in $W_0'$, is outside the maximal ideal; the element $\operatorname{jqNModC} k_0\,q - a_0$ lies in $K_0$ and in $O$, and $\iota$ carries it to a unit times $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$; there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_0$ containing $O$, inducing $A$ on $k_0$, which is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$, which admits an element $t$ such that for every polynomial over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$ whose value at $t$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ all coefficients already lie in that maximal ideal, which contains $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal, which reads off $R_0$-reductions in the sense that for every $g \in \operatorname{modularFunctionFieldFull} M'$ that is $R_0$-integral and has no pole where $\mathrm{jq}$ has none, the element $\operatorname{coeffEmb} k_0\,g$ lies in $K_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ precisely when its $R_0$-reduction vanishes, and, if that reduction lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ and differs by a non-unit of $O$ from the image of every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at the reduction; and for which every node other than $O$ contains an element outside $W_x$; and finally there is a subring $B_x$ of $K_0$ whose elements lie in $B_0$ and in $O$, all of whose elements have non-negative order at every place of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$ at which $j_\ell$ has non-negative order, such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at its non-units, $B_x$ has fraction field $K_0$, $B_x$ is generated as a subring by the image of $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite subset of $K_0$, and $B_x$ contains an element $b$ with the following separation property: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ inducing $A$ on $k_0$, with the image of $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, and such that (for $\operatorname{coeffEmb} k_0\,\mathrm{jq}$ regarded in $K_0$ and lying in $V$) no monic polynomial over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$ evaluated at it falls into the maximal ideal of $V$, if some element of $O$ lies outside $V$ then $b$ lies outside $V$.
--
--   This is the descent step in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ at a supersingular point in the small-prime case $q=2$, with the guard prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ used to rigidify the level: the $q+1$ ends of the rigid model upstairs, with their crossing presentations and Igusa branch data, are transported to the fixed field $K_0$ of the group generated by the level automorphisms of $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, where they become the $q+1$ node rings of the descended model. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd), which adds the inertia link to this package.
